WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.1 · Brand, Identity & Image
Brand, marketing and communications

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your brand is what people will expect from you; your image is what they think of you today.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Your brand is what people expect from you and associate with you. Identity, image, communications and marketing are related words, but each does a different job, and knowing which is which saves effort.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Different words, different jobs

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:39.722
Brand: What people expect from you and associate with you: what you stand for and promise. For example: A repair café known for friendly, practical help to fix things first.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:49.941
Identity: How you deliberately express the brand: name, voice and visual style. For example: A short name, the line “Fix first”, two colours and plain words.

7
00:00:49.941 --> 00:01:02.381
Image: What people actually think of you today, which may be very little at the start. For example: Early visitors call it “the friendly pop-up”; most people have not heard of it.

8
00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:13.800
Communications and marketing: Sharing information and stories; planned efforts to get a specific action. For example: A neighbourhood chat group, plus a campaign to find three volunteer electricians.

9
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:14.800
Why it matters

10
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.733
1. Without a clear brand, every message starts from zero.

11
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:25.778
2. The first people you serve need to know they will be safe.

12
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:32.081
3. Early customers, funders and partners look for credibility and values.

13
00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:33.081
What it guides

14
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:38.015
1. Your brand promise and platform, in the next lesson.

15
00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:43.319
2. Your voice, visual identity and guidelines, later in this module.

16
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.622
3. Your marketing and communications, built on top of the brand.

17
00:01:50.022 --> 00:01:50.622
What to avoid

18
00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:54.444
Thinking a logo is a brand.

19
00:01:54.444 --> 00:01:59.378
Leaving brand for later, as something only companies need.

20
00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:06.052
Describing the brand you want while ignoring what early reactions say.

21
00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:08.452
You describe your early image and the brand you want.

22
00:02:08.452 --> 00:02:12.452
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:17.052
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
